      "line": 28,
      "priority": "P2",
      "recommendation": "Reconcile unique PID/creation identities and covered lifetime charges across retained attempts, then enforce cumulative ceilings at admission and final verification. Preserve unobserved lifecycle fields as UNKNOWN.",
      "trigger": "The permitted continuation loop accumulates more than 3000 observed descendant starts or 21600 seconds of covered process lifetimes before another formal admission."
    },
    {
      "effect": "The logical-size check permits outputs that consume the required 256 MiB reserve, exceed task-wide storage during download/restoration, or create more than two complete archives. External outputs are outside the monitored root and have no cumulative accounting.",
